{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966796,"nonce":"+qoF/+AETmMaFqcQixQvYG1cP3k=","title":"render_overlay_msaa silently drops layer effects","message":"`render_overlay_msaa` (blinc_gpu/renderer.rs) doesn't walk\n`batch.layer_commands`, so any `LayerEffect` pushed via\n`ctx.push_layer(...)` was silently dropped on the no-glass MSAA\npath in `RenderContext::render_tree_with_motion`. The glass\nbranch already routes through `render_with_clear` whenever\n`has_layer_effects_in_batch` is true; the no-glass fast path\ndidn't, so MSAA + layer effects = invisible blur / shadow / glow.\n\n`use_msaa_overlay` is `RenderContext.sample_count \u003e 1` — the\nRenderContext defaults to 4× MSAA via `BlincApp.sample_count = 4`,\neven though the GPU renderer log line reports the inner\n`RendererConfig.sample_count = 1` (SDF pipelines are always\nsingle-sampled). Don't trust the startup log to tell you whether\nthe MSAA dispatch is live.\n\nFirst fix tried was `if use_msaa_overlay \u0026\u0026 !has_layer_effects`\nto keep MSAA on no-effect frames. That made blur visible but\nintroduced a per-frame flash whenever an animated effect (e.g.\n`breathe-blur` 0→32→0) crossed the no-op threshold — every\nboundary frame fell back to the MSAA overlay while every other\nframe ran the single-sampled effect path, and mesh-primitive\nsilhouette AA shifts visibly between hardware coverage and the\nSDF shader's barycentric ramp.\n\nFinal fix: pin the no-glass fast path to `render_with_clear`\nalways (commit `8d92007c`). Path geometry still gets MSAA via\n`render_paths_overlay_msaa` below. Mesh primitives use shader-\nside AA on every frame instead of toggling, eliminating the\nflash. Trade-off: mesh primitives no longer get hardware MSAA on\nno-effect frames, but the shader's barycentric AA is already\n1 px wide — visually equivalent for axis-aligned content and\nimperceptibly different for diagonals.\n\n**Why:** ruffle's m1 demo authored a `Node::effects: [Blur 32]` on\na `ShapePath::Rect`. The data made it all the way to `push_layer`\n(`ruffle DIAG` showed the Blur entries every frame at the right\nradii) but `apply_layer_effects` never ran. CSS-side blur\nappeared to work because every blur demo on the Blinc side also\ncontained backdrop / glass elements, which routed through the\nglass branch's `render_with_clear` dispatch.\n\n**How to apply:** When wiring any new layer effect or composite\nthat depends on `LayerCommand::Push`/`Pop`, exercise it on a\nno-glass scene with default MSAA on (a bare ruffle / canvas-kit\nsketch). If it disappears with `sample_count \u003e 1` but renders\nwith sample_count=1, the dispatch in\n`render_tree_with_motion` (or one of the other render entry\npoints) is bypassing layer commands. Fix is at the dispatch\nsite, not in the effect implementation.\n\nFixed in commit `da29258b` (\"fix(render): honour layer effects on\nthe no-glass MSAA fast path\").","files":null}]}